--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party programs oxAudit can invoke, and does not distribute
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Binary scanning runs whichever of these external programs you have installed.
oxAudit does not bundle, embed, link against, or redistribute any of them; it
executes a copy you installed yourself, at arm's length. No part of their
licensing attaches to oxAudit as a result.

  cve-bin-tool    GPL-3.0-or-later   https://github.com/ossf/cve-bin-tool
  grype           Apache-2.0         https://github.com/anchore/grype

docker/cve-bin-tool/Dockerfile is a build recipe, not a distribution. The image
it describes is built on your machine and fetches cve-bin-tool from PyPI there.
Do not publish a built image to a registry without meeting the GPL obligations
that would then attach to you.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Detection signatures
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The component signatures in src-tauri/src/binscan/native/signatures.toml are
original work. They were derived from binaries whose versions were known
independently, using tools/derive-signatures.py, and are deliberately not
transcribed from cve-bin-tool's checkers, which are GPL-3.0-or-later. See
docs/binary-signatures.md for the method and its provenance.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Methodology adopted from other projects
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Design ideas were studied and reimplemented from the projects below. No source
code was copied from any of them; what was adopted is method, which carries no
licence obligation. They are credited here because credit is owed.

  VulnHunter      Apache-2.0   https://github.com/capitalone/VulnHunter
                  Gate-based falsification triage and the candidate-manifest
                  silent-drop guard (src-tauri/src/triage/, docs/vulnhunter-study.md)

  VulHunt         MIT/Apache-2.0 for the BIAS crates, GPL-3.0 for the engine
                  https://github.com/vulhunt-re/vulhunt
                  Nibble-masked byte-pattern matching over binaries
                  (src-tauri/src/binscan/native/bytes.rs, docs/vulhunt-study.md)

  y-agent         Licence not asserted here — see upstream
                  https://github.com/gorgiaxx/y-agent
                  Design-system structure, the design-compliance test, the
                  ToolDefinition/registry shape, the bounded model-turn loop
                  with dual budgets, and the allow/ask/deny permission pipeline
                  (docs/design-system.md, docs/y-agent-adoption.md,
                  docs/y-agent-adoption-report.md)

                  oxAudit vendors no y-agent source. The study documents quote
                  short excerpts for commentary; nothing from the project is
                  compiled into or shipped with oxAudit.

